faqs.a:
The council, on behalf of the city and in its name, without any election, shall have
               power from time-to-time to acquire, improve, equip, operate and maintain, within or
               without the city, or both within and without the city, any project, including without
               limitation:
(1)
A combined sewer project;
(2)
A curb and gutter project;
(3)
A drainage and flood control project;
(4)
An off-street parking project;
(5)
An overpass project;
(6)
A park project;
(7)
A sanitary sewer project;
(8)
A sidewalk project;
(9)
A storm sewer project;
(10)
A street project;
(11)
An underpass project; and
(12)
A water project.
(Code 1981, § 27-7; Ord. No. 551, § 5, 5-14-1964; Ord. No. 1643, § 2, 2-18-1980)
State Law reference—
What improvements may be made, C.R.S. § 31-25-503.
